{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Custom LLM_CTL arm for chat_llm: runs a turn through the Claude Code CLI (the binary the Claude Agent SDK spawns) so inference draws on a Pro/Max subscription's OAuth login instead of metered API credits - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN are stripped from the child environment unless CLAUDE_CODE_ALLOW_API_KEY=on. Wire it with LLM=CLAUDECODE and LLM_CTL=agent:llm:claude_code. NOT a drop-in model provider: Claude Code runs its own agent loop with its own tools, so this always answers kind:text (never kind:tool_calls) and the passed `tools` are ignored - point CLAUDE_CODE_MCP at newbound's own MCP server to give the delegate the full store instead. PERMISSIONS: the CLI runs headless, so nobody can approve a tool call; when CLAUDE_CODE_MCP is set and CLAUDE_CODE_PERMISSION_MODE is anything but bypassPermissions, the arm adds --allowedTools mcp__<server> for every server named in the config (literal JSON or a path), so the configured servers' tools run in every mode and as root, where the CLI refuses bypass. Skipped when CLAUDE_CODE_ARGS carries its own --allowedTools, or with CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_ALLOW=off. There is no per-call confirmation. The conversation is flattened chat_llm-style (system messages become the system prompt, a lone user turn goes verbatim) and rides stdin, never argv. The CLI runs with --output-format stream-json, one JSON line per event, and two clocks bound it: CLAUDE_CODE_TIMEOUT is the hard wall clock, CLAUDE_CODE_IDLE_TIMEOUT (default 1200 s) kills a delegate that has gone silent; either kills the whole process group and the error names the clock. Config: CLAUDE_CODE_BIN, _MODEL, _EFFORT, _CWD, _TIMEOUT, _IDLE_TIMEOUT, _MCP, _PERMISSION_MODE, _AUTO_ALLOW, _TOOLS, _SYSTEM_MODE, _ARGS, _ALLOW_API_KEY. Replacing the default system prompt and disabling built-in tools is the default because it measured ~170x cheaper per turn. Returns the chat_llm envelope plus cost_usd, num_turns and session_id.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, Read, Write};\nuse std::sync::mpsc::{channel, RecvTimeoutError};\nuse std::thread;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n","params":[{"name":"messages","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"tools","type":"JSONArray"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"mqghlt1a00a71c647q1","readers":[],"time":1795265150622,"username":"system","writers":[]}